// The renderer firewall (proposal-attributes.md §5; ADR-35 D6): tooling,
// the REPL, and agents read attributes only through the reified
// `Report.attributes` projection — a plain-data field of `{ node, schema,
// payload, tier }` rows. A renderer reads that field and renders it; it parses
// nothing, lowers nothing, types nothing.
//
// Here the `doc` attribute on `greet` is resolved, checked against its `String`
// schema, and projected as one `Report.attributes` row — the row the harness
// reads back through the `expect-attribute` directive (the executable image of
// what an LSP hover or a REPL `:attrs` command would show).
//
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-def: greet
//@ expect-attribute: doc
@[doc("Returns a fixed greeting.")]
def greet = "hello";
